  h += 'Leave blank to <strong>auto-fit by model size</strong> so a local model stays fully on the GPU (16384 for gemma4:12b; 8192 for a 31B or 32B model on a 24GB card such as an RTX 4090; more for smaller models). This is the single biggest speed control: Ollama reserves GPU memory for the whole context up front, so too large a value spills the model to system RAM and conversions crawl (minutes become hours). Only set a number to override. <strong>Important:</strong> this field is applied over Ollama&apos;s native API, which the browser can only reach if <code>OLLAMA_ORIGINS</code> allows this site on a recent Ollama. If <code>ollama ps</code> still shows a CPU/GPU split after saving, set the context on the Ollama host instead, which always works: <code>setx OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH 8192</code> on Windows, <code>launchctl setenv OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH 8192</code> on a Mac, or <code>Environment="OLLAMA_CONTEXT_LENGTH=8192"</code> in the systemd unit on Linux (<code>sudo systemctl edit ollama</code>), then restart Ollama. To fit a larger context without spilling, also set <code>OLLAMA_KV_CACHE_TYPE=q8_0</code> the same way (roughly halves the memory the context uses). Confirm with <code>ollama ps</code>: it should read <code>100% GPU</code>.';
